WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.270
- You don't have to be
an asshole to succeed.

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:03.764
- This is true.

00:00:03.764 --> 00:00:05.330
- [Female Voice] Ladies and gentlemen,

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:06.749
your attention please.
- What the fuck?

00:00:06.749 --> 00:00:09.499
(alarms blaring)

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.430
- I thought we were out of
time, and I was just like--

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:16.263
- Yeah, me too!

00:00:16.263 --> 00:00:18.240
(both laughing)

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.679
Should I carry on?

00:00:19.679 --> 00:00:21.602
What was I gonna say after that?

00:00:21.602 --> 00:00:25.020
Hi I'm Gina, I'm here with
Bobby from Netflix's "Queer Eye"

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.850
and here are his Netflix Nine.

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:28.750
Okay so my first question to you

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.360
is going to be about "Queer Eye."

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.193
- Okay.

00:00:31.193 --> 00:00:33.220
- Which is your favorite
"Queer Eye" episode?

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:34.500
- People ask me that all the time

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:35.680
and I don't have a favorite baby.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.160
We have a least favorite baby,

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.700
but we don't have a favorite baby.

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:40.810
- Can I tell you my favorite

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:42.000
episode with you?
- Yeah.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.640
- Hold on, because I only
just recently watched it.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:45.980
Thank you so much, thank you.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:47.390
One with, I think it's Rob.

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:48.537
And he's a widower
- Oh, Rob and his sons.

00:00:48.537 --> 00:00:51.020
- and the two sons.
- Yes, Rob Elrod.

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:51.853
He is such a sweet man.

00:00:51.853 --> 00:00:54.084
- But you were just so gorgeous
in that episode and so nice.

00:00:54.084 --> 00:00:54.917
- Aw!

00:00:54.917 --> 00:00:55.870
- I know!

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:56.770
Maybe I'm just buttering you up

00:00:56.770 --> 00:00:58.622
'cause I really want you
to be my best friend.

00:00:58.622 --> 00:01:01.180
If you could swap homes
with any celebrity,

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:02.800
who would you choose?

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:03.714
- The queen.

00:01:03.714 --> 00:01:04.547
- Oh, really?

00:01:04.547 --> 00:01:05.380
- Yeah, I mean who wouldn't wanna

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:06.213
live in the palace?
- Oh yeah, I guess so!

00:01:06.213 --> 00:01:07.290
- Yeah, yeah, I guess.
- The best house out there.

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:09.970
- Don't you feel intimidated
by the amount of rooms?

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:13.090
How many rooms does it have
in the palace, like 600?

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:14.233
I made that up.

00:01:14.233 --> 00:01:15.300
- Buckinham Pa--
- No no no, I made that up.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.650
- Actually, Mandy Moore's house,
have you seen it recently?

00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:19.220
- Yes, oh my God!

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:21.320
- Which, we have the same pool guy.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:23.716
The guys that built hers
is building mine right now.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:24.549
- Oh really?

00:01:24.549 --> 00:01:27.040
- So I'm hoping that mine
just looks just even slightest

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:28.290
bit like Mandy Moore's.

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:30.510
- Her house's awesome and
she's the sweetest woman ever,

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:31.450
- She's so nice.
- But her house looks

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:33.320
beautiful, totally my style.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:36.450
- And if you could decorate
any celebrity's home,

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.330
who would it be, or you
could have a celebrity

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:40.920
decorate your home, either/or.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.680
- Probably wouldn't want
anyone to touch mine.

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:44.458
- Okay that is absolutely fair.

00:01:44.458 --> 00:01:45.983
(both laughing)

00:01:45.983 --> 00:01:49.240
- I don't know, I never know
who any celebrities are.

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:50.073
- Oh.

00:01:50.073 --> 00:01:51.527
- I always get the same question,

00:01:51.527 --> 00:01:53.440
"What celebrity do you wanna make over?"

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:56.107
And I'm like, "Oh, ya know,"
I try to spin it with,

00:01:56.107 --> 00:01:57.967
"Ya know, we don't
really make people over,

00:01:57.967 --> 00:01:59.456
"we try to make them better."

00:01:59.456 --> 00:02:00.897
And she's like, "All right,

00:02:00.897 --> 00:02:02.460
"well who do you wanna make better?"

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:03.767
And then I was like, "I don't know.

00:02:03.767 --> 00:02:05.292
"I don't know who anybody is."

00:02:05.292 --> 00:02:08.220
And she's like, "What
about Cole blah blah blah?"

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:11.180
Cole somebody, I don't know,
he was some Disney star.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:12.013
- Oh, Cole Sprouse?

00:02:12.013 --> 00:02:12.846
Riverdale?
- Yes!

00:02:12.846 --> 00:02:13.840
She's like, "What about Cole Sprouse?"

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:15.060
And I'm like, "I don't know who that is."

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:16.619
She's like, "He's standing
right next to you."

00:02:16.619 --> 00:02:20.260
(Gina laughs loudly)

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:21.922
Hi! (laughing)

00:02:21.922 --> 00:02:24.671
- That is so embarrassing!

00:02:24.671 --> 00:02:26.280
"Hi, I'm Bobby, nice to meet you."

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:28.053
- Yeah, I don't know who that is!

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:32.010
- So how long, when
you're making over homes,

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:34.161
you're doing home projects,
how long does it actually take

00:02:34.161 --> 00:02:35.048
for you to do that

00:02:35.048 --> 00:02:35.960
for each?
- I get the home on Tuesday

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:39.100
afternoon and I have it
back by Friday morning.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:40.990
- I just don't underst-- okay.

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:41.823
- Magic.

00:02:43.099 --> 00:02:45.347
- But you don't even plan or anything?

00:02:45.347 --> 00:02:46.200
- Oh no there's planning.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:47.033
- Okay.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.250
- And the thing is I go out

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:49.810
a few weeks before the other boys.

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:50.643
- Oh, I see.

00:02:50.643 --> 00:02:53.310
- And I get a warehouse and
I just buy tons of stuff,

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:54.820
and I kinda make my own store.

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:57.392
- When I spoke with Tan, few months ago,

00:02:57.392 --> 00:03:00.287
he said his biggest
inspiration was Michelle Obama.

00:03:00.287 --> 00:03:01.430
And I was watching--

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:03.500
- He told me that I was
his biggest inspiration.

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:05.400
- It was a lie, I'm so sorry (laughs).

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:07.318
He told me Michelle Obama, I--

00:03:07.318 --> 00:03:09.047
- Well mine's Barack Obama!

00:03:09.047 --> 00:03:10.447
- Yeah, well that's what
I was gonna ask you.

00:03:10.447 --> 00:03:11.280
- It actually is.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:12.900
- Yeah, I saw an interview that said

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.107
that yours was Barack Obama,

00:03:14.107 --> 00:03:15.605
and I wanted to ask if that's true.

00:03:15.605 --> 00:03:16.980
- Yes
- Why Barack?

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:17.813
- Why?

00:03:17.813 --> 00:03:20.020
- I mean, I love you, Barack, but I--

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:20.853
- Why?

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:25.136
Just because of everything
he represents, the hope,

00:03:25.136 --> 00:03:29.134
the kindness, the
generosity, the intelligence,

00:03:29.134 --> 00:03:30.490
I mean, everything.

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:33.460
Karamo met him and he borrowed
one of my suits to wear

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:36.000
when he went to meet him,
and Barack gave him a hug,

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.163
and so I'm like (sniffing),
Barack's touched my suit!

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:44.559
The other day, I was having
lunch with Oprah, no big deal.

00:03:44.559 --> 00:03:46.594
(both laughing)

00:03:46.594 --> 00:03:50.500
And we were at the first
annual Empowerment Awards

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:51.820
and she was getting an award.

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:53.131
Everything that was
coming out of her mouth,

00:03:53.131 --> 00:03:56.270
I'm just like sitting at
the table trying not to cry

00:03:56.270 --> 00:03:57.513
at a luncheon in Hollywood.

00:03:57.513 --> 00:03:58.863
- Yeah.

00:03:58.863 --> 00:04:01.970
- If she ran for president, she would win,

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:04.290
but I can also understand why
she doesn't want to because--

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:05.550
- No, I get it too.

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:07.490
- She does so much good in the world

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:08.740
and does what she wants to do.

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:10.230
And when you're president,

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:11.840
your hands are tied in so many ways.

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:12.673
- Yeah.

00:04:12.673 --> 00:04:14.200
- I think she does more for the world

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.270
as just Oprah than President Oprah.

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:18.100
- I actually just wanted to
say that earlier you said

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:20.240
that you don't know many celebrities,

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:22.910
and then you've just said that
you had brunch with Oprah.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:25.536
So, ya know what, fair, I love that.

00:04:25.536 --> 00:04:26.793
(both laughing)

00:04:26.793 --> 00:04:28.280
That's how I wanna be, I love that a lot.

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:30.504
So, what's something about British culture

00:04:30.504 --> 00:04:32.293
that you particularly like?

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:35.617
- How direct people are.

00:04:35.617 --> 00:04:37.860
- Oh really, you think we're direct here?

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:40.890
- Well I mean, some people say
direct, some people say rude,

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:42.690
some people say tomato,
some people say tomato.

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:45.211
- Okay. (laughs)

00:04:45.211 --> 00:04:47.851
- But that's one thing we
can always count on with Tan,

00:04:47.851 --> 00:04:49.990
he'll flat out tell you the truth.

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:51.077
We're like, "Tan is this cute?

00:04:51.077 --> 00:04:51.910
"No."

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:53.650
- Okay, okay, that's true.

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:55.270
And what's something about British culture

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:56.900
that you don't understand?

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:59.110
- The humor.

00:04:59.110 --> 00:04:59.943
- Really?

00:04:59.943 --> 00:05:02.483
- I don't understand why it's funny.

00:05:02.483 --> 00:05:04.287
(both laughing)

00:05:04.287 --> 00:05:06.220
- "Queer Eye" is a groundbreaking show,

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:08.810
in terms of LGBTQ representation.

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:11.930
Is being a part of that
representation important to you?

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:12.860
- Absolutely.

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:14.323
- Why do you think it matters?

00:05:14.323 --> 00:05:15.740
- I think it matters because

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:17.570
growing up as the little
gay boy in Missouri,

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:19.200
I didn't have that representation.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:23.130
I didn't have people to
show me that A, it was okay,

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:26.143
B, that I would be okay,
and that I could make it,

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:28.890
that I'd be able to get out of there

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:30.380
and be able to live a normal life,

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:31.590
just like any other person.

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:32.970
So I think that's why it's important

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:36.180
to have that representation,
for the younger generation

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:38.623
to be able to see that you're okay.

00:05:38.623 --> 00:05:40.357
- Absolutely
- And you'll be okay.

00:05:40.357 --> 00:05:44.040
- Okay so what are three
things you can't live without?

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:47.903
- Sad, but my phone because
it runs my world, coffee,

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:50.580
and ...

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:51.980
- That's very American.
- My husband.

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:52.813
- Aw!

00:05:54.374 --> 00:05:55.207
All right, we get it.

00:05:55.207 --> 00:05:56.040
Love it real
- I was like,

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:57.526
"I'm either gonna say
bacon or my husband."

00:05:57.526 --> 00:05:59.960
(both laughing)

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.567
- Hard to say, depends what day.

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:05.590
- Either way, they're yummy.

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:08.180
- Okay so, I don't wanna
put you on the spot,

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:11.580
but I spoke to one of your
other members of "Queer Eye,"

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:14.290
and when I asked about the
sixth member of "Queer Eye,"

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:15.750
he said he would choose me.

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:17.110
I'm not saying that you should choose me

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:18.490
to be the sixth member of "Queer Eye,"

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:20.930
but if you were to choose
anybody to be the sixth member.

00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:21.843
- It would be you.

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:25.890
- Thanks, that's all I wanted to hear.

00:06:25.890 --> 00:06:26.723
- We're done.

00:06:26.723 --> 00:06:27.956
- Yeah, we're done, do you
want me to ask some more?

00:06:27.956 --> 00:06:28.884
- Yeah, I want some more.

00:06:28.884 --> 00:06:31.172
- Well, ya know, it's only nine
questions, isn't it, babes?

00:06:31.172 --> 00:06:33.156
(both laughing)

00:06:33.156 --> 00:06:35.260
Netflix nine hours of
me and you just talking.

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:37.561
- Yeah, Netflix Nine ...

00:06:37.561 --> 00:06:38.394
Hours.

00:06:38.394 --> 00:06:40.210
(both laughing)

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:43.627
( peaceful guitar music)

